1
00:00:00,079 --> 00:00:01,419
A man insulted Jesus behind His back.

2
00:00:02,079 --> 00:00:03,199
Jesus complimented him to his face.

3
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:04,880
Philip told Nathanael the news:

4
00:00:05,259 --> 00:00:06,919
the Messiah — Jesus, of Nazareth.

5
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:07,960
Nathanael's answer:

6
00:00:08,519 --> 00:00:10,199
"Can there any good thing come out

7
00:00:10,239 --> 00:00:11,921
of Nazareth?" Philip did not argue —

8
00:00:11,979 --> 00:00:12,439
he invited.

9
00:00:13,279 --> 00:00:13,920
Jesus spoke first:

10
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,779
"Behold an Israelite indeed, in whom is

11
00:00:17,879 --> 00:00:19,219
no guile!" Nathanael asked:

12
00:00:19,979 --> 00:00:21,859
"Whence knowest thou me?" Jesus answered:

13
00:00:22,379 --> 00:00:24,819
"Before that Philip called thee, when thou

14
00:00:24,899 --> 00:00:27,319
wast under the fig tree, I saw

15
00:00:27,399 --> 00:00:29,379
thee." A moment only heaven had seen

16
00:00:29,399 --> 00:00:29,799
— named.

17
00:00:30,679 --> 00:00:31,439
The doubt did not fade.

18
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:32,319
It fell.

19
00:00:32,979 --> 00:00:33,419
Nathanael said:

20
00:00:33,939 --> 00:00:36,380
"Rabbi, thou art the Son of God;

21
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:40,059
thou art the King of Israel." And

22
00:00:40,119 --> 00:00:41,799
Jesus went further:

23
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:44,379
"Thou shalt see greater things than these...

24
00:00:45,039 --> 00:00:47,860
Hereafter ye shall see heaven open, and

25
00:00:47,899 --> 00:00:50,619
the angels of God ascending and descending

26
00:00:50,719 --> 00:00:52,299
upon the Son of man." That is

27
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:53,779
Jacob's ladder — the one Jesus said

28
00:00:53,819 --> 00:00:55,719
He is, standing open, permanently.

29
00:00:56,459 --> 00:00:57,699
He is not offended by honest questions.

30
00:00:58,099 --> 00:00:59,359
He already sees you, under your fig

31
00:00:59,419 --> 00:00:59,599
tree.

32
00:01:00,539 --> 00:01:00,919
Come and see.
